WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.730
What did the doctor say?

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.690
That there's nothing wrong with me.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.730
That it must be psychological.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.740
But if I stop smiling, I feel like
 my anxiety will crush me.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.990
I'm not the real Re:vale.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.460
Discover...

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.500
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.680
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:29.700
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.040
Wow...

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:45.690
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.780
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:55.530
No matter what tomorrow's 
like, it won't betray us

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:01.240
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.870
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.410
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:11.660
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.420
Discover...

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.220
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.850
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.180
Night sky

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:28.100
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.520
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:36.150
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.450
Wow...

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.000
#10 Out of Time

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:57.010
You're not the "real" Re:vale?

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.590
What does that mean?

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.300
It's exactly...

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.720
what it sounds like.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:09.550
We act like we've been friends for ten 
years and like we're a married couple,

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.320
but in reality, we're not.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.860
I was Yuki—Yuki-san's fan.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:17.950
A fan?

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.740
We're sorry for pushing back the filming.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.940
It's all right.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.500
Re:vale always does so much to help us out.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.370
More importantly, is Momo-kun okay?

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.190
I don't know.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.090
You don't have any idea what's causing it?

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:41.080
That's the first time I've 
seen Momo-san yell at you.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:45.180
What did Momo-san mean when he said that?

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.150
That's he's out of time.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.440
When Yuki was an indie artist, he 
worked as Re:vale with someone else.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.570
Someone else?

00:02:58.830 --> 00:02:59.620
Yeah.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:04.380
They wrote songs and sang together.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:08.580
They did everything together.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.150
They were so cool.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.640
Male idols have a lot of female fans, but they 
were also popular among men, including me.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.770
I admired the two of them and 
followed them everywhere.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.280
I loved them. I loved Re:vale.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.170
How did Re:vale end up in
its current form, then?

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.070
Did this person and Yuki-san have a fight?

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:42.590
No. They got along great.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.800
They respected and recognized 
each other's talent.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:51.750
That's when a famous producer 
reached out to Re:vale.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.060
A famous producer...

00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:01.010
Yeah. I've forgotten his name, 
but he was Zero's manager.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.550
Zero's manager? That's amazing!

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:08.020
But they turned down his offer.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.980
What? Why?

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.880
Because of a difference in artistic direction.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.550
They planned to find an agency
 that would let them

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.360
do things their own way, 
and would debut with them.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:25.240
But just before their debut, Yuki-san's 
partner had an accident onstage.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.200
An accident?

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:29.340
I was watching that concert.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:35.120
A ceiling light suddenly fell 
from directly above Yuki-san.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.920
His partner protected him.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.350
When he came to his senses...

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.550
The concert was canceled.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:53.060
His partner survived, but it 
left a nasty scar on his face.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.730
Is it even possible for a light to fall?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.180
Are you sure someone didn't 
cause the accident?

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.940
The possibility came up, yeah.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.380
People said it was someone 
jealous of Re:vale's popularity

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.570
or a staff member who was 
upset about being reprimanded.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:15.330
In any case, the agency rescinded their
 offer to help them debut after that.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:21.340
But the famous producer made them an offer.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.870
He'd introduce them to a hospital that could 
remove the scar on his partner's face.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:30.280
And in exchange, he wanted 
them to go with him.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:33.390
So those were his terms.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.270
Just like Tenn-nii.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.010
He told them they had talent.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.160
That they could surpass Zero 
and become legends themselves.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:47.720
Feeling responsible for his 
partner's scarred face,

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.780
Yuki-san readily accepted his offer.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:53.000
Wasn't their artistic direction
too different, though?

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:58.460
Yeah. Yuki-san's partner was 
probably worried about that.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:03.890
He wanted Yuki to find someplace where 
he could sing his way. Re:vale's way.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:07.890
Leaving behind that message, he disappeared.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:10.180
No way...

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:13.960
Yuki-san was really depressed at the time.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.660
I couldn't bear to watch.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:22.400
He searched desperately for his 
partner, but couldn't find him.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.260
Yuki-san was considering retirement.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:33.340
When I heard he was quitting 
music, I had to do something.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.140
I asked Yuki-san

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.290
not to quit singing.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.670
Over and over and over again.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:54.050
I asked him to make me his temporary partner.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.150
"It can be just until you find your partner."

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:01.300
"It can be for only the five 
years you worked with him."

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.480
"But please form a group with me."

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:06.480
"Please."

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:11.080
"I don't want you to quit singing."

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:14.940
Momo-san...

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:21.640
I begged him with a face 
full of snot and tears.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.210
Even I was disgusted with myself.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.110
But Yuki's a gentleman, you know?

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:35.320
At first, he said he couldn't 
imagine working with anyone else.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:39.440
But one morning, after I'd been
 visiting for a month,

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:43.770
he said yes.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.280
Since that day, it's been like a dream.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:55.070
I'm singing with the man I looked up to.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:58.620
We share our worries like friends.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.910
We've received a ton of awards.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:08.340
But this happiness doesn't belong to me.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.220
The current Re:vale

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.090
isn't the real Re:vale.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.540
That's not true.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:17.810
Tenn-nii...

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:21.500
Re:vale's current fans are 
fans of you and Yuki-san.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:26.970
The current Re:vale is the dream
 you and Yuki-san seized.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.120
I thought the same thing.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.630
That Re:vale was Yuki and me.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:37.660
But Yuki's still searching for his partner.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:43.020
I overheard him asking someone to 
find him by our fifth anniversary.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.130
You mean...

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:49.860
I asked Yuki to let me work 
with him for five years.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.670
You get it, don't you?

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:56.200
On our fifth anniversary, 
I'll run out of time.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:00.200
At the very least, that's how Yuki feels.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:07.600
That's not how I feel.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:15.320
That's not how I feel.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:17.570
Yuki...

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:22.200
That's what you were worried about?

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:25.640
That's why you couldn't sing?

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.040
Well...

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:31.170
Momo-san, you're wrong.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.830
Yuki-san just wants his 
former partner to come

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.790
because it's an important concert.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:40.220
He thinks of you as his real partner.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.930
Right, Yuki-san?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.680
Well, I suppose I do.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.800
You suppose? Why don't you tell 
him that clearly, then?

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.920
That no one can replace him.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:55.100
That he's your only partner now and forever.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:10:00.410
Gaku-kun, unlike the sexiest man 
alive, I'm easily embarrassed.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.260
I'm shy, too!

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.330
You're definitely not.

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:05.370
You don't have to force it.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.790
You're just too nice to abandon me.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.750
That's not true.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.850
You'd rather perform with your 
former partner, wouldn't you?

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.130
That's not—

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.470
See? You hesitated!

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.900
No, no. I nearly sneezed.

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.120
You always dodge the question!

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:26.020
I know you spend every night 
looking at old photo albums!

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.570
My friend is missing.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.690
Let me be a little sentimental.

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:35.200
Sometimes you say, "<i>He</i> could've done that!"

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.310
I don't say that.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:37.360
You do!

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.070
Then I'm sorry for that.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:41.610
It's fine! You don't have to apologize!

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:44.240
You still have a lingering attachment 
to your old partner, right?

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.610
Don't you?

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:48.580
Well, yeah. I'd be lying if I denied it.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.380
See? You do!

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:53.140
That's the same as cheating!

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:55.520
I'm going back to my parents' place!

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:58.700
Don't, honey. Not in front of the kids.

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.840
What are you guys arguing about, exactly?

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:05.090
I understand how Momo-san feels, though.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:08.420
Being compared to the partner he 
respected would come as a shock.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:09.090
Riku...

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:09.980
You think so?

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.780
I think Momo-san's being a little cowardly.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.170
Even if you're compared to someone else,

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:18.810
as long as you don't think you're 
worse, you should be fine.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.200
What's up with all you people winning at life?

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.650
Tenn-nii, you don't get it.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:29.410
Since you could always do everything, I never
 got to be number one at anything.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:29.750
What?

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:35.750
I made all the time I could to look 
after you, and now you're giving me this?

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.130
"Tenn-nii, I love you!"

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.490
So, you said things like that while 
being secretly annoyed with me?

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.470
Isn't that a bit extreme 
for a dual personality?

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.970
Like you're one to talk.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:48.790
I-I'm grateful, but there were 
also things I didn't enjoy!

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:51.220
Iori, back me up!

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:55.500
If I had to choose, I'd say my feelings are 
closer to Yaotome-san and Kujo-san's.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.610
Do you want me to disagree with you?

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:01.900
Damn it! If Mitsuki were here, 
he'd understand...

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.280
Then let me ask you this.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:07.450
Do you know what it's like to take care of
 someone, only to have them complain?

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:07.940
That.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:08.910
Seriously, that.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.120
I'm not complaining!

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.260
We're lamenting that you guys 
don't understand our feelings!

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:14.770
What do you want me to do, then?

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:18.840
Do you want me to look at pictures of you 
as much as I've looked at pictures of him?

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:22.090
Receiving love like it's routine 
work doesn't make me happy!

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.840
You don't get it at all!

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.050
Yeah!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.930
You're the ones who don't get it.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:27.220
Huh?

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:33.620
I sacrificed myself to look after my precious, 
sickly little brother so he could be happy.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:37.500
Then he suddenly showed up one 
day and declared he'd surpass me.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:40.440
Have you ever considered how <i>that</i> feels?

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.360
W-Well, I...

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:45.880
When you put it that way, 
I feel sorry for you.

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:48.150
Don't you? Be nice to me, then.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.590
There, there.

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.990
Yuki-san, you don't have any intention of

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:55.380
replacing Momo-san as your 
partner in Re:vale, right?

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:56.570
I don't.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:59.820
That's a relief, then. 
There's nothing to worry about.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.450
Right, Momo-san?

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:04.630
Yeah, but...

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:08.890
Were you unable to sing 
because I made you anxious?

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.610
I don't know...

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:18.650
Sing, Momo. I'm genuinely sorry.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:22.150
I want to hear you sing.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:24.510
Yuki...

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.750
Gaku-kun, what did you say earlier?

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.090
Until the day the world ends,

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:33.620
you're the only partner in the universe 
that I want, now and forever.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:37.330
Have you made it even more embarrassing?

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.560
Not really. Isn't that normal?

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:39.790
It's not normal.

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:45.170
Until the day the world ends,

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:49.680
you're the only partner in the universe 
that I want, now and forever.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:51.590
Really?

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:53.770
Yeah. Let's go back to the studio.

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:55.890
Think you can sing?

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:58.400
Yeah.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:00.940
Great!

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:02.840
Now it's a happy ending.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.560
Let's hurry back.

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:37.280
What's wrong with me?

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:41.020
You still don't trust Yuki-san?

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:47.810
I think I trust him, but maybe somewhere 
in my heart I still doubt him.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:52.530
After all, Yuki is so calm and collected.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:58.060
The only time I saw him lose his composure 
was when his partner left him.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.800
Even if I work with him for ten more years,

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:07.180
I have a feeling I won't ever see Yuki

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:10.660
get that upset over me.

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.220
What's wrong with him?

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:22.480
Maybe he still senses your 
attachment to your old partner.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:26.110
It's not attachment.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:31.860
I think it's guilt that I alone experienced 
success without ever repaying the favor.

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:36.160
Is it possible that Momo-san
 is being drugged?

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:37.840
Drugged?

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:40.350
You've been reading too many mystery novels.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.110
You haven't heard?

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:46.440
Since Re:vale announced they'd 
be covering Zero's song...

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:48.380
Oh, that graffiti...

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:52.420
It was on the news.
There were even witnesses.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:55.510
Witnesses? You mean who saw the vandals?

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:58.390
It was some guy cosplaying as Zero.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.980
He was even wearing a mask.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:04.120
Apparently he even performed Zero's songs.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.080
Zero himself, huh?

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:13.980
Is the legendary idol angry with us?

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:18.100
Whether it's really him or not, 
I don't like what he's doing.

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:21.520
You're still going to cover Zero's song?

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:22.830
For now.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.450
Don't you feel bad for 
songs that aren't sung?

00:16:30.310 --> 00:16:31.990
Drugs, huh?

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.870
I'll keep an eye out.

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:41.930
Sogo, Tamaki.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:45.570
Evening.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:46.780
Good evening.

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:49.150
You guys are recording now?

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:49.820
Yeah.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:52.360
Nagicchi, what's wrong?

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:55.140
Does your stomach hurt or something?

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:59.600
Oh, Tamaki. Listen to this.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:05.110
My heart is currently as 
fragile as cracked glass.

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:08.320
Don't worry about him. He's just pouting.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.000
What?!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:14.100
Nagi-kun, are you still sulking because 
Mitsuki-san was cast in <i>Magical Cocona</i>?

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:17.930
It's disgraceful for a man 
to be jealous, Nagicchi.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.350
Should you be saying that?

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:23.140
Oh, God! Why have you forsaken me?

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:26.980
Was my love insufficient?

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:31.860
But there's nothing this 
beautiful man can't do!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:32.820
Okay, okay.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:36.600
By the way, did you guys hear about Momo-san?

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:39.980
Yes. I'm worried.

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:43.490
Crap. I think I forgot 
my phone in the greenroom.

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:45.310
What are you doing?

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:46.460
I'll go get it.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:48.170
So-chan, wait for me outside.

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:49.210
Okay.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:56.300
This place...

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:03.370
<i>I should tell Tamaki-kun about that girl.</i>

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:08.230
<i>He could probably stay calm and listen now.</i>

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:11.560
Don't move.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:16.200
Don't make a sound.
I have a question for you.

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:22.520
Have you seen the key chain I dropped 
when we met here the other day?

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:24.810
If you have it, please return—

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:30.970
I'm certain now.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:33.340
You're Tamaki-kun's sister, Aya-chan!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.110
The way you jump to 
extremes is just like him!

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:38.240
N-No, I'm not! What are you talking about?

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:40.260
Why won't you meet Tamaki-kun?

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.890
He became an idol specifically to find you!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.400
He's on his way. Wait here while—

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:44.970
I can't!

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:48.400
Why not?

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:51.480
I can't do anything to betray him.

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:53.410
"Him"?

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.110
My benefactor.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.660
He's kind, like in Jean Webster's
 <i>Daddy-Long-Legs</i>.

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:02.010
I want to live up to his expectations.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:04.080
You can't meet with Tamaki-kun 
because you want to

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:05.700
live up to your benefactor's expectations?

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:07.080
That's right.

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:10.570
Someone who won't let them see 
their family isn't a kind person.

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:12.650
If you're in trouble, we'll help—

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:14.530
I'm not the one in trouble!

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:21.900
I want to help <i>him</i>.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:22.960
Aya-chan?

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:26.330
He's hurt.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:30.140
He's lost his precious light.

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:34.240
He's hurt. He's suffering.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:38.660
He's trying to achieve his dream again.

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:42.990
I want to help make his dream come true.

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:50.330
But... I'm probably just the backup.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:54.010
He's probably entrusting his dream to...

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:03.130
It's TRIGGER.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:06.510
You're right. Kujo Tenn is so cool.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.800
Kujo Tenn?

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:11.920
Aya-chan, what—

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:21.710
So-chan, thanks for waiting.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:27.760
What? You look like you've seen a ghost.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:28.450
Huh?

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.630
So-chan?

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:33.400
Tamaki-kun, there's something 
I need to tell you.

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:34.310
Hey, it's MEZZO".

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:38.000
Which one's Yotsuba Tamaki, the guy 
who sent someone to the hospital?

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.760
Don't. They'll hear you.

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:42.290
Apparently it's because they used 
his sister to mess with him.

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:44.330
So-chan, let's go.

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:45.480
Huh?

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:50.190
Tamaki-kun...

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:53.530
The meeting for the drama was interesting.

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:55.730
The director seems nice.

00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:00.860
I think I might like this job.

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:09.940
<i>If I tell Tamaki-kun about Aya-chan,
will he abandon his work like before?</i>

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:13.550
<i>I don't want to hear people 
criticize him anymore.</i>

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:17.640
<i>Maybe I shouldn't tell him until 
the situation becomes clearer.</i>

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:22.820
<i>But the whole reason Tamaki-kun 
became an idol was to find Aya-chan.</i>

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:26.270
<i>Should I let him prioritize her?</i>

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:29.850
<i>And besides that...</i>

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.020
So-chan?

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:43.940
<i>Besides that, will Tamaki-kun quit 
being an idol if he finds Aya-chan?</i>

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:47.110
What? Is there something you want to say?

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:50.410
<i>Should I tell him or not?</i>

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:52.160
Hey, So-chan.

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:54.540
<i>What's better for Tamaki-kun?</i>

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:58.150
You're not going to tell me?

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:02.550
You can be like this sometimes. Jeez...

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:09.530
<i>What should I do? What should I...</i>

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:19.450
What should I do?

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:27.080
Why?

00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:30.200
Why is this happening?

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:37.460
(You are never far from my heart...)

00:22:34.210 --> 00:22:36.820
Tell me, Yuki.

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:40.530
What should I do?

00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:44.270
(You are never far from my heart...)

00:22:44.270 --> 00:22:50.440
When my feelings were like a desert

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:58.040
You kept on watering them

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:03.650
What's the name of the flower that blooms

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:10.970
The moment you smile?

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:17.840
As my hands gently sway at the 
lingering scent of that day

00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:28.070
Let's look up at the new sky
 -What color is it?-

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:36.670
I wish I could tell you exactly how I feel

00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:42.900
But when our eyes meet, my 
embarrassment gets in the way

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:50.180
This Melody that sets my 
heart on fire is telling me

00:23:50.180 --> 00:23:58.100
That there's a tomorrow that 
I can only create with you

00:23:57.300 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:57.300 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"The Place I Want to Protect"</b>
